From: Bruce Ashfield <bruce.ashfield@gmail.com>
Subject: [PATCH] fs/aufs: route the FUSE mnt-ns check back through is_current_mnt_ns

The aufs6.18 refresh moves fs/aufs to the native upstream snapshot, whose
vfsub.c calls our_mnt() directly. Upstream exports our_mnt() via its own
standalone integration patch; our integration instead exports a small
is_current_mnt_ns() wrapper. The refresh delta reverted that carried
adaptation, leaving an unexported our_mnt() reference that fails to link
whenever aufs is compiled.

Restore it: route the CONFIG_AUFS_BR_FUSE mnt-ns check back through
is_current_mnt_ns(). Unlike v7.x, 6.18 does not need the open-coded
rename-lock helpers -- lock_rename()/unlock_rename() are still exported in
the 6.18 kernel (the unexport landed upstream in v7.1).

Signed-off-by: Bruce Ashfield <bruce.ashfield@gmail.com>

diff --git a/fs/aufs/vfsub.c b/fs/aufs/vfsub.c
index f456fe7171891..96df3cc7bb6af 100644
--- a/fs/aufs/vfsub.c
+++ b/fs/aufs/vfsub.c
@@ -33,7 +33,7 @@ int vfsub_test_mntns(struct vfsmount *mnt, struct super_block *h_sb)
 	if (!au_test_fuse(h_sb) || !au_userns)
 		return 0;
 
-	return our_mnt(mnt) ? 0 : -EACCES;
+	return is_current_mnt_ns(mnt) ? 0 : -EACCES;
 }
 #endif
 
